{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"reviews\":[{\"id\":\"structural_monotony\",\"verdict\":\"insufficient_evidence\",\"rationale\":\"The document does have recurring expository paragraph shapes, but the annotator gave no section-level evidence showing the repeated arc across multiple parts of the piece.\",\"evidence\":[\"Most respondents reported that their usual health professional was aware of important aspects of their medical history.\",\"However, gaps were more apparent when patients moved between services.\",\"Continuity was associated with better reported experiences.\",\"The findings support continued work to improve secure information exchange, discharge communication and accountability for follow-up.\"]},{\"id\":\"tonal_uniformity\",\"verdict\":\"insufficient_evidence\",\"rationale\":\"The register appears consistently formal and policy-analytic, but the annotator did not supply textual evidence demonstrating that the register holds throughout the document.\",\"evidence\":[\"The national survey provides new information about how Australian patients experience coordination between different parts of the health system.\",\"These differences warrant further investigation because poor coordination can compound existing barriers to care.\",\"They complement administrative and clinical data by showing how arrangements are experienced by the people using them.\"]},{\"id\":\"faux_specificity\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"The document stays general and institutional; it does not use decorative pseudo-specific detail of the kind this registry item targets.\",\"evidence\":[\"Respondents were asked about communication among health professionals, follow-up after hospital care, access to information and the support they received in managing ongoing conditions.\",\"Some respondents said they had to repeat their medical history because information had not reached a new provider.\"]},{\"id\":\"neutrality_collapse\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"The text takes a clear position that coordination problems exist and that improvement work should continue, rather than flattening into both-sides balance.\",\"evidence\":[\"These differences warrant further investigation because poor coordination can compound existing barriers to care.\",\"The findings support continued work to improve secure information exchange, discharge communication and accountability for follow-up.\"]},{\"id\":\"even_jargon_distribution\",\"verdict\":\"overcall\",\"rationale\":\"The vocabulary is consistently appropriate to a health-policy summary, but it is not suspiciously uniform jargon for its own sake; it mixes technical and plain phrasing naturally.\",\"evidence\":[\"coordination between different parts of the health system\",\"timely advice about medicines, warning signs or the next stage of care\",\"They complement administrative and clinical data by showing how arrangements are experienced by the people using them.\"]},{\"id\":\"forced_synesthesia\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"There are no cross-modal metaphors mapping senses onto abstractions or emotions.\",\"evidence\":[\"These experiences can cause inconvenience and anxiety and may increase the risk of duplicated tests or avoidable treatment.\",\"They also underline the value of regular primary-care relationships.\"]},{\"id\":\"generic_metaphors\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"The prose is largely literal and report-like; it does not rely on generic metaphorical framing as a substitute for concrete meaning.\",\"evidence\":[\"The survey measures patients’ perceptions rather than clinical outcomes and does not establish why particular failures occurred.\",\"patient reports identify practical points at which coordination succeeds or breaks down\"]},{\"id\":\"referential_clarity\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"Pronouns and definite descriptions have recoverable antecedents in context, and the prose does not show excessive vague-reference drift.\",\"evidence\":[\"These findings indicate that information sharing works effectively for many people\",\"These differences warrant further investigation because poor coordination can compound existing barriers to care.\",\"They complement administrative and clinical data by showing how arrangements are experienced by the people using them.\"]},{\"id\":\"formulaic_parallelism\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"The document uses ordinary enumeration, but not slogan-like symmetry or repeated corrective scripts standing in for content.\",\"evidence\":[\"communication among health professionals, follow-up after hospital care, access to information and the support they received in managing ongoing conditions\",\"medicines, warning signs or the next stage of care\"]},{\"id\":\"semantic_redundancy\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"The paragraphs develop related points, but no sentence merely restates nearby information without adding a new distinction or implication.\",\"evidence\":[\"However, gaps were more apparent when patients moved between services.\",\"Patients with complex needs had more contact with the health system and therefore more opportunities to encounter coordination problems.\",\"Continuity was associated with better reported experiences.\"]},{\"id\":\"underspecified_language\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"The annotator correctly identified vague evaluative phrases whose criteria are not defined in the passage.\",\"evidence\":[\"well-connected care\",\"mixed experiences\",\"timely advice\",\"more consistent experiences across patient groups\"]},{\"id\":\"context_leakage\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"The document does not answer an absent interlocutor or defend itself against missing chat context; it reads as standalone prose.\",\"evidence\":[\"The results show that many patients experienced well-connected care, but coordination was not consistent across the population.\",\"Nevertheless, patient reports identify practical points at which coordination succeeds or breaks down.\"]},{\"id\":\"performed_candour\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"There are no candour-performance markers such as \\\"frankly,\\\" \\\"honestly,\\\" or similar authenticity boosters.\",\"evidence\":[\"The survey measures patients’ perceptions rather than clinical outcomes and does not establish why particular failures occurred.\",\"Future survey cycles will allow changes to be monitored\"]},{\"id\":\"vacuous_connection\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"Connectors such as \\\"However\\\" and \\\"Nevertheless\\\" mark clear contrasts, and the coordinated clauses generally state their relationships explicitly.\",\"evidence\":[\"However, gaps were more apparent when patients moved between services.\",\"Nevertheless, patient reports identify practical points at which coordination succeeds or breaks down.\"]},{\"id\":\"genre_specific\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"This text fits the registry's default bucket better than the named genres, and no genre-specific watchlist issue is triggered within that classification.\",\"evidence\":[\"The national survey provides new information about how Australian patients experience coordination between different parts of the health system.\",\"The findings support continued work to improve secure information exchange, discharge communication and accountability for follow-up.\"]}]}"}}
